<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-PacMags to buy out Indonesia partner.</title>
<headline>RTRS-PacMags to buy out Indonesia partner.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pacific Magazines and Printing Ltd said on Tuesday that it had made arrangements to buy out its Pac-Rim Kwartanusa Printing business in Indonesia.</p>
<p>PMP chief executive Ken Catlow told the company's annual meeting that the group had made arrangements to purchase its partner's 40 percent holding in the Indonesian company.</p>
<p>He gave no more details.</p>
<p>The move follows Australia's decision in its 1996/97 budget to scrap the book bounty scheme, which Catlow described as a blow to the Australian publishing industry.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
